# Experiment B: Hadoop and Spark burst with EMR managed scaling, tier S data (Phase 15, Wave 1).
# UNAPPROVED and UNEXECUTED. Format: scripts/README.md, "Experiment manifest contract".
# No spaces in values.
# PLACEHOLDERS the human replaces before an approval record is written
# (the record binds the sha256 of the final file, so any edit needs a new record):
#   ACCOUNT_ID       123456789012 is the documented example, not a real account.
#   (DATASET_SNAPSHOT is filled: scholarchain-s-20261107-10dd7f34121b, reported by WO-4 and
#                    verified by the human.)
#   OUTPUT_ROOT      /abs/outside/repo/... is a placeholder path; pick a durable directory
#                    outside the repository.
# Needs the tier S overlay plus infra/terraform/environments/course/elasticity-s.tfvars
# (primary 1, core 1, managed scaling Min 1, Max 3, core-only: the limits count core and task
# nodes only, doc-verification.md K2, so at most 4 instances in all; Neptune off, Bedrock off,
# a bounded wait before the cluster is terminated). Check the On-Demand Standard vCPU quota
# first (4 x m5.xlarge = 16 vCPUs; applied quota 32, doc-verification.md). The loader command
# in the execution input is a no-op, see experiments/b-burst/README.md.
# Limits (tier S caps of decision P15-1: 90 min, 64 clients, 20000 tasks; at the cap, P15-16):
#   MAX_MINUTES 90   the full tier S cap (decision P15-16, review 1 K1: the earlier 80 min limit
#                    with a 74 min pipeline stop left about 140 s of slack in the realistic
#                    case). The pipeline script inside the entry point stops at 88 min
#                    (experiments/b-burst/run.sh), strictly below this limit.
#   MAX_CONCURRENCY 1, MAX_TASKS 1: the entry point starts exactly one pipeline execution. The
#                    unit of MAX_TASKS here is one start-execution; the script cannot enforce it.
# Cost basis: HOURLY_BURN_USD 1.55 is the highest-capacity rate: 4 instances x 0.35 + 8
# interface endpoints x 0.015 + loader task 0.0247 (UNVERIFIED rates, COST_ESTIMATE.md).
# 1.55 x 90 min / 60 = 2.325, so the ceiling is 2.40 (P15-16). Session 1 HIGH is about 3.15 USD
# in all (decision P15-16); this manifest bounds the entry-point window only.
MANIFEST_VERSION=1
EXPERIMENT_ID=B
DESCRIPTION=hadoop-spark-burst-managed-scaling-tier-s-core1-to-3-wait-before-terminate
ENVIRONMENT=course
REGION=us-east-2
ACCOUNT_ID=123456789012
DATASET_SNAPSHOT=scholarchain-s-20261107-10dd7f34121b
SIZE_TIER=S
MAX_MINUTES=90
MAX_CONCURRENCY=1
MAX_TASKS=1
SPEND_CEILING_USD=2.40
HOURLY_BURN_USD=1.55
STOP_CONDITIONS=wall-clock,first-failure,spend-estimate
METRIC_NAMES=ExecutionTime,ExecutionsFailed,AppsPending,ContainerPending,ContainerPendingRatio,TotalNodesRequested,TotalNodesRunning,TotalUnitsRequested,TotalUnitsRunning,CoreNodesRunning,TaskNodesRunning,YARNMemoryAvailablePercentage
METRIC_NAMESPACES=AWS/States,AWS/ElasticMapReduce
OUTPUT_ROOT=/abs/outside/repo/scholarchain-experiments
ENTRY_POINT=script:experiments/b-burst/run.sh
